# a member that takes no receiver, read through another unit's type path with
# no argument written, is a call with no receiver: `staticmk.Counter.fresh`
# emitted the path itself as the call's first argument, and the C did not
# compile. With every parameter defaulted, with none at all, on a record, as a
# member read's base and in statement position.
main: function is {
    a: staticmk.Counter.starting
    print "starting \{a.n}"
    b: staticmk.Counter.fresh
    print "fresh \{b.n}"
    print "read \{staticmk.Counter.starting.n}"
    s: staticmk.spot.at
    print "at \{s.x}"
    staticmk.Counter.fresh
    c: staticmk.Counter.starting start: 3
    print "given \{c.n}"
}
